body:
Assignments with 0 instances were stuck in Upcoming with no way to remove them. Finalized assignments had no explicit archival mechanism. This PR adds soft-delete (via `active: false`) for both cases.

## Changes

### `computeLane()` — routing fix
- 0-instance assignments with `active === false` now route to `'finalized'` instead of `'upcoming'`

```js
if (instances.length === 0) {
  if (assignment.active === false) return 'finalized';
  return 'upcoming';
}
```

### `renderUpcomingCard()` — Delete button
- "Delete" button (red) added to cards with 0 instances
- `rcConfirm({ danger: true })` → `db.updateAssignment(id, { active: false })` → local state patch → re-render

### `renderFinalizedEntry()` — Archive button + Archived badge
- Active finalized entries get an "Archive" button (muted style)
- Entries with `active === false` display an "Archived" pill badge instead

### `showAssignmentDetail()` modal — context-aware action
| Context | Action |
|---|---|
| Upcoming, 0 instances | "Delete" button (danger) |
| Finalized, active | "Archive" button |
| `active === false` | Static "Archived ✓" indicator |

### Tests
- Mirrored `computeLane()` in `tc-library-helpers.test.cjs` updated to match
- Added: `'no instances + active=false → Finalized'`

