## PR #834 Retry — Add delete/archive functionality for individual library assignments

The previous PR #834 was closed due to ESLint lint failures. This is a retry. **The code MUST pass ESLint.** Base off current `main` (commit `49ff286a8b7367381acbe0399d35c509e3131949`).

### ESLint rules to follow (from `.eslintrc.json`)

The project ESLint config enforces these rules on `site/web/*.js`:

1. **`no-restricted-globals` (ERROR level for `site/web/*.js`)**: Do NOT use `alert()` or `confirm()`. Use `rcAlert()` and `rcConfirm()` instead (these are declared as globals in the config).
2. **`no-unused-vars` (WARN level, but causes CI failure at error count)**: Every declared variable must be used. No unused variables. Pattern `^_` is allowed for intentionally unused args/vars.
3. **No `window.alert()` or `window.confirm()`** — use `rcAlert(title, message)` and `rcConfirm(title, message, confirmLabel, options?)` which are globally available from `rc-modal.js`.

### What to change

Only modify **`site/web/tc-library.js`**. Do NOT modify `data-adapter.js` or any other files.

### Change 1: Update `computeLane()` (around line 781)

Current code:
```js
function computeLane(assignment, allInstances) {
    const instances = allInstances.filter(i => i.assignment_id === assignment.id);
    if (instances.length === 0) return 'upcoming';
    // ...
}
```

Change to:
```js
function computeLane(assignment, allInstances) {
    const instances = allInstances.filter(i => i.assignment_id === assignment.id);
    if (instances.length === 0) {
      if (assignment.active === false) return 'finalized';
      return 'upcoming';
    }
    // ... rest unchanged
}
```

